#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114884 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ce098ff9-2ef1-5483-b057-b3fef12af16d" :question/math-academy-id "e-2477" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $\\mathbf f(t) + 2\\mathbf g(t)$ with respect to $t,$ where $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)$ are defined as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =(4{t}^{2}+9)\\,i-(\\frac{1}{t-2})\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,k \\\\ g(t) & =(4t-1)\\,i+{e}^{3t}\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf f(t) + 2\\mathbf g(t))' = \\mathbf f'(t) + 2\\mathbf g'(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivative of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{2}+9)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{1}{t-2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)\\,k \\\\  & =8t\\,i+\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k, \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-1)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{3t})j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)k \\\\  & =4\\,i+3{e}^{3t}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+2g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+2{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(8t\\,i+\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k)+2(4\\,i+3{e}^{3t}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k) \\\\  & =8(t+1)\\,i+(\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}+6{e}^{3t})\\,j-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114885 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b19f5f01-948e-5f44-8016-63073ed31dbc" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Scalar Function Multiple Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3668609c-7f98-53ef-8aa7-6f9c3209dfee" :question/math-academy-id "e-2478" :question/problem "Find $\\big( u(t) \\mathbf g(t) \\big)'$ where $[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t) = t.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\big( u(t) \\mathbf g(t) \\big)' = u'(t) \\mathbf{g}(t) + u(t) \\mathbf{g}'(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find $\\mathbf g'(t)$ and $u'(t),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)g(t))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)g(t)+u(t){g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+t\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -t \\\\ 2t{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -2t \\\\ (2t+1){e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114886 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a146d5d3-2562-5b8b-886e-4cf6519d3282" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Chain Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cbb15346-028c-59c0-9b20-cd2f408c3bcb" :question/math-academy-id "e-2479" :question/problem "Find $(\\mathbf f \\circ u)'(t),$ if $\\mathbf f(u) = \\ln u \\, \\mathbf i + (u^2+5) \\, \\mathbf j + 4u \\, \\mathbf k$ and $u(t) =2t^3.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(\\mathbf f \\circ u)'(t) = \\mathbf{f}'(u(t)) u'(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivative of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡u)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({u}^{2}+5)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(4u)k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\,i+2u\\,j+4\\,k, \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3})=6{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{u(t)}\\,i+2u(t)\\,j+4\\,k){u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2{t}^{3}}\\,i+2(2{t}^{3})\\,j+4\\,k)\\cdot 6{t}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{t}\\,i+24{t}^{5}\\,j+24{t}^{2}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114887 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54a6dbe-42cb-5614-ae0b-611de1719b45" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Product Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "228ae66f-9dad-5e6d-b405-9fbe62ecb7e9" :question/math-academy-id "e-2480" :question/problem "Find $\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt} (\\mathbf f \\cdot \\mathbf g)(t),$ given the following functions $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =\\sqrt{t}\\,i+{t}^{2}j \\\\ g(t) & =\\frac{1}{t}i+{e}^{t}j\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Using the dot product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f} \\cdot \\mathbf{g})(t) = \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f}(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf{g}(t) + \\mathbf{f}(t) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{g}(t))\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}f(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\,i+2t\\,j, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}g(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})j \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt} (\\mathbf f \\cdot \\mathbf g)(t)\n&= \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f}(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf{g}(t) + \\mathbf{f}(t) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{g}(t)) \\[3pt]\n&= \\left(\\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}} \\,\\mathbf i +2t \\, \\mathbf j \\right) \\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{1}{t} \\,  \\mathbf i + e^t \\,  \\mathbf j \\right) +\n\\left(\\sqrt{t} \\,  \\mathbf i + t^2 \\,  \\mathbf j \\right) \\cdot \\left(-\\dfrac{1}{t^2}  \\, \\mathbf i + e^t \\, \\mathbf j  \\right) \\[3pt]\t\t \n&=\\dfrac{1}{2t\\sqrt{t}}  +2te^t    +  \\left(-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{t^2}\\right)    + t^2e^t \\[3pt]\n&=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{2t^2}  -  \\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{t^2} +2te^t   + t^2e^t  \\[3pt]\n&= -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{2t^2} +\\left(2t+t^2\\right)e^t.\n}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305615 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6272e646-6faf-5cbf-9aa8-bfa1c9a1a5a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,-2t,\\,2t-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305617} {:answer/id #uuid "61492250-b27b-5c47-b317-b118914c4bd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,2t,\\,{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305618} {:answer/id #uuid "41c31433-12c8-5113-bb33-8079400d618f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,\\,2t+1,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305619} {:answer/id #uuid "12a7c4c0-521d-5b22-8f03-585838f052b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305620} {:answer/id #uuid "2fc264b1-b837-534c-ae0b-bb800191e149" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fc264b1-b837-534c-ae0b-bb800191e149" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305621} :answer-field/id #uuid "41aec396-46ce-51ab-bf41-4cb56972babe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305616}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1e49dfe3-04a3-591e-9ea0-48737f115840" :question/math-academy-id "q-127998" :question/problem "Differentiate $f(t)+g(t)$ with respect to $t$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨1-2t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,(t-1)^{2}⟩, \\\\ g(t) & =⟨t+1,\\,1-2t,\\,{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "By the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f(t)+g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((t-1)^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2t,\\,2(t-1)⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-2,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2t,\\,2t-2⟩+⟨1,\\,-2,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305622 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "666d0943-d962-5343-b8b8-584d547cecb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\pi ,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305742} {:answer/id #uuid "2bf663e2-ab37-5760-8f98-b6bf2245f3c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305743} {:answer/id #uuid "40b45b28-7d4c-5c26-acf2-22c77fbe8a93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305744} {:answer/id #uuid "7f5fcda8-94e0-5680-9724-baadb419019e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,4\\pi ,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305745} {:answer/id #uuid "c7f74fa6-e400-517d-b831-8393b1be5955" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,1,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305746}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2bf663e2-ab37-5760-8f98-b6bf2245f3c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305743} :answer-field/id #uuid "67fc88b4-87c5-5184-9df4-c543d7d6b38d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305741}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0cef1288-682b-5449-bd6c-f4cbfcbde18f" :question/math-academy-id "q-128452" :question/problem "Find the value of $(2f(t)-g(t))^{′}$ at $t=-1,$ if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨8\\sqrt{3-t},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t),\\,\\ln|2t|⟩, \\\\ g(t) & =⟨{t}^{2}-t,\\,\\pi {t}^{2},\\,1-{t}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since $t=-1$ lies in an open interval where $t<0$ and $3-t>0$, all components are differentiable there. In particular, $\\ln|2t|=\\ln(-2t)$ near $t=-1$, so its derivative is $1/t$.\n\nDifferentiate each vector component:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf f'(t)=\\left\\langle-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{3-t}},\\pi\\cos(\\pi t),\\frac1t\\right\\rangle,\n\\qquad\n\\mathbf g'(t)=\\langle 2t-1,2\\pi t,-2t\\rangle.\n$$\n\nThe sum and constant multiple rules give\n\n$$\n(2\\mathbf f-\\mathbf g)'(t)=2\\mathbf f'(t)-\\mathbf g'(t).\n$$\n\nAt $t=-1$,\n\n$$\n\\mathbf f'(-1)=\\langle-2,-\\pi,-1\\rangle,\n\\qquad\n\\mathbf g'(-1)=\\langle-3,-2\\pi,2\\rangle.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n(2\\mathbf f-\\mathbf g)'(-1)\n=2\\langle-2,-\\pi,-1\\rangle-\\langle-3,-2\\pi,2\\rangle\n=\\boxed{\\langle-1,0,-4\\rangle}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305629 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33682dc1-7836-5315-acfc-61983cb7e073" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305631} {:answer/id #uuid "93f4968d-77ca-532e-ab00-5ef5419b3d74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -15 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305632} {:answer/id #uuid "03c79f25-da83-5144-b27e-06ae9a5ad549" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305633} {:answer/id #uuid "e034714c-afd7-5ce7-adb3-22f0570a983c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305634} {:answer/id #uuid "eda74f62-92e9-558c-94d6-262daf7dc797" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33682dc1-7836-5315-acfc-61983cb7e073" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305631} :answer-field/id #uuid "78e86278-ed9e-5659-9814-700204a333be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305630}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d53a4971-40a3-5d73-9c6b-7c763e59097b" :question/math-academy-id "q-128458" :question/problem "Find the value of $(2f(t)+5g(t))^{′}$ at $t=1,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{3+t} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-1) \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2t-3 \\\\ {t}^{2} \\\\ (t+1)^{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "By the sum rule, we have \n \n\n$$\n(2f(t)+5g(t))^{′}=2{f}^{′}(t)+5{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\,(2\\sqrt{3+t}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-1)) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3+t}} \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1) \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-3) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((t+1)^{2})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2t \\\\ 2(t+1)\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence , we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2f(1)+5g(1))^{′} & =2{f}^{′}(1)+5{g}^{′}(1) \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3+1}} \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1-1) \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+5[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2(1) \\\\ 2(1+1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+5[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305636 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b19f5f01-948e-5f44-8016-63073ed31dbc" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Scalar Function Multiple Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c44db689-2e72-5d37-a789-ef9aaf267cde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,5t\\sqrt{t},\\,3\\sqrt{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305638} {:answer/id #uuid "e86dbad6-c367-5b18-b949-a66a00630e64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t,\\,\\sqrt{t},\\,\\sqrt{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305639} {:answer/id #uuid "810eba93-bafe-55fa-946a-f1cd36da1086" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{2},\\,5\\sqrt{t},\\,3{t}^{2}\\sqrt{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305640} {:answer/id #uuid "992afb58-96db-50ba-a119-ed5b31ddfea7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,5t\\sqrt{t},\\,3\\sqrt{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305641} {:answer/id #uuid "a2f00692-91aa-5bed-a81d-6aa2758406e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,2t\\sqrt{t},\\,\\sqrt{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305642}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "992afb58-96db-50ba-a119-ed5b31ddfea7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,5t\\sqrt{t},\\,3\\sqrt{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305641} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f44686b-d66f-52c3-85fa-0a4c59229667" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305637}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2f602a22-c320-5e1b-8210-46c053005f25" :question/math-academy-id "q-128477" :question/problem "Find  $(u(t)g(t))^{′}$ where $g(t)=⟨\\sqrt{t},\\,{t}^{2},\\,t⟩$ and $u(t)=2\\sqrt{t}.$" :question/worked-solution "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n \n\n$$\n(u(t)g(t))^{′}=u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${g}^{′}(t).$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,2t,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\sqrt{t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)g(t))^{′} & =u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{t}⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,2t,\\,1⟩+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}}⟨\\sqrt{t},\\,{t}^{2},\\,t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,4t\\sqrt{t},\\,2\\sqrt{t}⟩+⟨1,\\,t\\sqrt{t},\\,\\sqrt{t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,5t\\sqrt{t},\\,3\\sqrt{t}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305643 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a146d5d3-2562-5b8b-886e-4cf6519d3282" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Chain Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1688504-491d-5ed1-977d-71a2be217a97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,-\\frac{t}{2+{t}^{2}},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305645} {:answer/id #uuid "83e2f4cf-588a-592d-9565-6a6c5ef07e7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},-\\frac{{t}^{2}}{1+{t}^{2}},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305646} {:answer/id #uuid "eb1bba33-58b4-5a00-b06a-ff91a11fd24a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-\\frac{1}{t+{t}^{2}},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305647} {:answer/id #uuid "4e255fc7-6272-5f92-82e3-d5da680cb14a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{t},-\\frac{1}{t+{t}^{2}},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305648} {:answer/id #uuid "c3894f94-e78d-54bc-9274-7c41774f70f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-\\frac{t}{1+{t}^{2}},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb1bba33-58b4-5a00-b06a-ff91a11fd24a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-\\frac{1}{t+{t}^{2}},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305647} :answer-field/id #uuid "00777e8c-8742-506c-8fd2-c313410fdbd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305644}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "00ec801b-e22a-5c19-899f-45b6911ab4a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-128570" :question/problem "If $g(u)=⟨\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+1),\\,1⟩$ and $u(t)=\\frac{1}{t}$, then $(g∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(g∘u)^{′}(t)=g′(u(t))u′(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(u) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\frac{1}{u}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+1)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{u+1},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})=-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(g∘u)^{′}(t) & =g′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{(u(t))^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{u(t)+1},\\,0⟩\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨-{t}^{2},\\,\\frac{t}{1+t},\\,0⟩\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}) \\\\  & =⟨1,-\\frac{1}{t+{t}^{2}},0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305650 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54a6dbe-42cb-5614-ae0b-611de1719b45" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Product Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50dc45cb-e55b-52f4-a52b-5bece1dec1ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,3{t}^{2},\\,{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305652} {:answer/id #uuid "29a1d4dc-da17-5066-9630-3494aaf14753" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1,\\,3t,\\,{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305653} {:answer/id #uuid "85521d67-6236-51ea-8ce7-d15513094f2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,3{t}^{2},\\,\\sqrt{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305654} {:answer/id #uuid "3e4de446-e262-5377-9584-38c04d82f392" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1,\\,3{t}^{2},\\,2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305655} {:answer/id #uuid "dc1fd693-aa78-5dfd-a34d-37c50e3cef97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1,\\,t,\\,3t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305656}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e4de446-e262-5377-9584-38c04d82f392" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1,\\,3{t}^{2},\\,2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305655} :answer-field/id #uuid "63cfc577-b71b-52e8-a8a3-1261487aa5c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305651}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bf8c3fb4-2777-54a7-8b95-c44fdfa25968" :question/math-academy-id "q-128586" :question/problem "Find $(v(t)f(t))^{′}$ given that  $f(t)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,t⟩$ and $v(t)=2t.$" :question/worked-solution "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n(v(t)f(t))^{′}=v(t){f}^{′}(t)+{v}^{′}(t)f(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${v}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{t},\\,2t,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(v(t)f(t))^{′} & =v(t){f}^{′}(t)+{v}^{′}(t)f(t) \\\\  & =2t⟨\\frac{1}{t},\\,2t,\\,1⟩+2⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,4{t}^{2},\\,2t⟩+⟨2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2{t}^{2},\\,2t⟩ \\\\  & =2⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1,\\,3{t}^{2},\\,2t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305657 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54a6dbe-42cb-5614-ae0b-611de1719b45" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Product Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d708fa5-55b2-5152-8aaa-26338dd6cb84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{4},\\,{t}^{3},\\,{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305659} {:answer/id #uuid "eb032af8-4753-5ccb-8d9c-fe6e52cbfdd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t,\\,5{t}^{3},\\,9{t}^{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305660} {:answer/id #uuid "3875e15b-7b54-591c-a1ea-95ddfd8b539a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t,\\,5{t}^{4},\\,3{t}^{5}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305661} {:answer/id #uuid "86827724-76b1-54de-aa37-b7f9adb2fc3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4{t}^{3},\\,5{t}^{2},\\,9{t}^{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305662} {:answer/id #uuid "81ac5ec6-6a72-5ffd-88df-5fc2b2b99163" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4{t}^{3},\\,5{t}^{4},\\,12{t}^{5}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81ac5ec6-6a72-5ffd-88df-5fc2b2b99163" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4{t}^{3},\\,5{t}^{4},\\,12{t}^{5}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305663} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6d9e1d3-65a6-5f96-b7c3-5deec932ff21" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305658}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9d5f8c70-9278-5162-973d-4d7fea2c16c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-128587" :question/problem "Find  $(u(t)g(t))^{′}$ where $g(t)=⟨t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,2{t}^{3}⟩$ and $u(t)={t}^{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n(ug(t))^{′}=u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${g}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2t,\\,6{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})=3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)g(t))^{′} & =u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t) \\\\  & ={t}^{3}⟨1,\\,2t,\\,6{t}^{2}⟩+3{t}^{2}⟨t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,2{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{3},\\,2{t}^{4},\\,6{t}^{5}⟩+⟨3{t}^{3},\\,3{t}^{4},\\,6{t}^{5}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4{t}^{3},\\,5{t}^{4},\\,12{t}^{5}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305664 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54a6dbe-42cb-5614-ae0b-611de1719b45" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Product Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a27ec2ea-c098-5486-8483-fa7df003a644" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5{t}^{6},\\,{t}^{5}+4{t}^{2},\\,4{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305666} {:answer/id #uuid "9e01d9a9-2a90-5a58-9d87-627daa5da8c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{6}-5,\\,4{t}^{5}+2t,\\,4{t}^{3}-10t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305667} {:answer/id #uuid "07f384ad-9b9f-524a-9131-9ac57b5fbc9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2{t}^{6}+1,\\,4{t}^{5},\\,{t}^{3}-5t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305668} {:answer/id #uuid "25744ee0-8070-50f2-9184-27b0c4af738b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-7{t}^{6}+5,\\,6{t}^{5}-2t,\\,4{t}^{3}-10t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305669} {:answer/id #uuid "9bb993ab-caa1-5bbc-a46e-6b91afb5baad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨7{t}^{6},\\,6{t}^{5}-5,\\,4{t}^{3}+2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25744ee0-8070-50f2-9184-27b0c4af738b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-7{t}^{6}+5,\\,6{t}^{5}-2t,\\,4{t}^{3}-10t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305669} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ad2398b-cb23-53c5-a1bc-3850caae08ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305665}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c21f1368-688b-50ed-bde8-7422d801bdbd" :question/math-academy-id "q-128896" :question/problem "Find $(f\\times g)^{′}(t)$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨t,\\,5,\\,{t}^{4}⟩, \\\\ g(t) & =⟨{t}^{2},\\,{t}^{3},\\,t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the cross product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n(f\\times g)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(t)\\times g(t)+f(t)\\times {g}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,4{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,3{t}^{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t)\\times g(t) & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4{t}^{3} \\\\ {t}^{2} & {t}^{3} & t\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4{t}^{3} \\\\ {t}^{3} & t\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4{t}^{3} \\\\ {t}^{2} & t\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ {t}^{2} & {t}^{3}\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =⟨-4{t}^{6},\\,4{t}^{5}-t,\\,{t}^{3}⟩, \\\\ f(t)\\times {g}^{′}(t) & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ t & 5 & {t}^{4} \\\\ 2t & 3{t}^{2} & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & {t}^{4} \\\\ 3{t}^{2} & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}t & {t}^{4} \\\\ 2t & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}t & 5 \\\\ 2t & 3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =⟨5-3{t}^{6},\\,2{t}^{5}-t,\\,3{t}^{3}-10t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f\\times g)^{′}(t) & =⟨-4{t}^{6},\\,4{t}^{5}-t,\\,{t}^{3}⟩+⟨5-3{t}^{6},\\,2{t}^{5}-t,\\,3{t}^{3}-10t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-7{t}^{6}+5,\\,6{t}^{5}-2t,\\,4{t}^{3}-10t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115677 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54a6dbe-42cb-5614-ae0b-611de1719b45" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Product Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b029f1f-9e4a-597b-ae77-3d81c480f110" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60t^{3} + 15t^{2} + 14t + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113463} {:answer/id #uuid "cc3d915b-79a3-5034-a5de-c06db5adfc1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80t^{3} + 6t^{2} + 10t + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113464} {:answer/id #uuid "24835394-1f04-511b-a157-cfeb639fa83e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80t^{3} + 11t^{2} + 12t + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113465} {:answer/id #uuid "63aa8e90-8b39-5545-99b0-87f760920652" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60t^{3} + 7t^{2} + 10t + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113466} {:answer/id #uuid "7641f374-6267-5333-85c6-aaff569336a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80t^{3} + 15t^{2} + 10t + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7641f374-6267-5333-85c6-aaff569336a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80t^{3} + 15t^{2} + 10t + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113467} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f83259c-d6e0-5a5d-835f-1cdded5c1c51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113462}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a209f44d-4003-53ab-9d12-642d62514eb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-32298" :question/problem "Find $(f\\cdot g)^{′}(t)$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =20t\\,i-2t\\,j+(2+5t)\\,k \\\\ g(t) & ={t}^{3}\\,i+t\\,j+({t}^{2}+t)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Using the dot product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n(f\\cdot g)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(t)\\cdot g(t)+f(t)\\cdot {g}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(20t)\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2+5t)\\,k \\\\  & =20\\,i-2\\,j+5\\,k \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+t)\\,k \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}\\,i+j+(2t+1)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f\\cdot g)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(t)\\cdot g(t)+f(t)\\cdot {g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(20\\,i-2\\,j+5\\,k)\\cdot ({t}^{3}\\,i+t\\,j+({t}^{2}+t)\\,k)+(20t\\,i-2t\\,j+(2+5t)\\,k)\\cdot (3{t}^{2}\\,i+j+(2t+1)\\,k) \\\\  & =(20{t}^{3}-2t+5({t}^{2}+t))+(60{t}^{3}-2t+(2+5t)(2t+1)) \\\\  & =80{t}^{3}+15{t}^{2}+10t+2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115680 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a146d5d3-2562-5b8b-886e-4cf6519d3282" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Chain Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "949b7128-ac58-5a19-abd5-c446c6404838" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4t + 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113481} {:answer/id #uuid "a8e4e4cc-e41d-5275-8aba-ebb9127b417e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8t \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113482} {:answer/id #uuid "b3daaa61-1c5d-5b40-a9c2-237c16f4b80a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4t + 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113483} {:answer/id #uuid "c2e8a3fc-9fe9-55c1-9eed-507c1f94395c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8t + 8 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113484} {:answer/id #uuid "f3877b5f-6bb4-5d78-857c-eb8775ebe075" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2t \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2e8a3fc-9fe9-55c1-9eed-507c1f94395c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8t + 8 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113484} :answer-field/id #uuid "9cbc99ba-cc6c-5ec4-b8b5-c85bedb17f42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113480}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0fd1def5-bd75-572c-939f-770f964a1db9" :question/math-academy-id "q-32498" :question/problem "If $f(u)=[\\begin{aligned}2u \\\\ {u}^{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)=2t+2$, then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(2u) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\,({u}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(3)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2u \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t+2)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & =f′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2u(t) \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2(2t+2) \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8t+8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305671 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cebd29e4-87cb-572b-af0f-e2f507cdff45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2t,0,2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305673} {:answer/id #uuid "86b9e636-95ff-5f96-96da-479f305b5e98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2t-1,0,2t+1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305674} {:answer/id #uuid "95fe6746-9e7e-5186-8569-90337a4cf20b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305675} {:answer/id #uuid "33425daf-de81-52c8-a41e-ea1040b0a9d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨t-1,0,t+1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305676} {:answer/id #uuid "aa876634-6b62-550b-b0a0-cf726acb311d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t+1,2t+1,2t+1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86b9e636-95ff-5f96-96da-479f305b5e98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2t-1,0,2t+1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305674} :answer-field/id #uuid "23a8d32d-d998-5d9c-8f0b-312896fbb02c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305672}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8795bddd-70ad-516e-a9a3-68891cf5e70d" :question/math-academy-id "q-32503" :question/problem "Differentiate $f(t)+g(t)+h(t)$ with respect to $t$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨-1,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ g(t) & =⟨-t,\\,0,t⟩ \\\\ h(t) & =⟨-{t}^{2},0,{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f(t)+g(t)+h(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t)+{h}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,1⟩ \\\\ {h}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2t,\\,0,\\,2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+g(t)+h(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t)+{h}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩+⟨-1,0,1⟩+⟨-2t,\\,0,\\,2t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2t-1,\\,0,\\,2t+1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305678 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54a6dbe-42cb-5614-ae0b-611de1719b45" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Product Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1256526b-0b63-5849-ba74-47a5ae991c40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305680} {:answer/id #uuid "ca2411e2-bdce-546a-ab4b-2d46ff1b9b3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305681} {:answer/id #uuid "0a79529c-5c53-5eef-866f-9e91c6e4d092" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305682} {:answer/id #uuid "f750d2e5-0984-584e-bf6c-4a6db0237a73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305683} {:answer/id #uuid "bbc82d85-4371-53f6-b5fc-69fcb54c1cc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305684}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a79529c-5c53-5eef-866f-9e91c6e4d092" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305682} :answer-field/id #uuid "d90a3398-318a-588b-8110-fc4ea12ba2c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305679}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d5473c95-fbd9-54b5-ab3e-4d48d13acc31" :question/math-academy-id "q-32837" :question/problem "Given $f(t)=({t}^{3}-1)\\,i+({t}^{2}-2)\\,j+4{t}^{2}\\,k$, evaluate $({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(0).$" :question/worked-solution "Using the dot product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(t)={f}^{″}(t)\\cdot f(t)+{f}^{′}(t)\\cdot {f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the first and second derivative of the function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-1)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-2)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}\\,i+2t\\,j+4\\cdot 2t\\,k \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}\\,i+2t\\,j+8t\\,k \\\\ {f}^{″}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8t)\\,k \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2t\\,i+2j+8\\,k \\\\  & =6t\\,i+2j+8\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(0) & ={f}^{″}(0)\\cdot f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)\\cdot {f}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =(6(0)\\,i+2\\,j+8\\,k)\\cdot (({0}^{3}-1)\\,i+({0}^{2}-2)\\,j+4(0)^{2}\\,k)+(3(0)^{2}\\,i+2(0)\\,j+8(0)\\,k)\\cdot (3(0)^{2}\\,i+2(0)\\,j+8(0)\\,k) \\\\  & =(2\\,j+8\\,k)\\cdot (-i-2\\,j) \\\\  & =0(-1)+2(-2)+(0) \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305685 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a146d5d3-2562-5b8b-886e-4cf6519d3282" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Chain Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42b63046-d0c8-5b17-a680-40625cee930b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{u} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2u\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305687} {:answer/id #uuid "ce329a3c-d6dc-516e-8f1d-f962832405f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305688} {:answer/id #uuid "059f6fed-d4b0-5135-99a2-3f4b6890742c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305689} {:answer/id #uuid "f210782f-76de-5c66-920d-d343470da810" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305690} {:answer/id #uuid "5291c699-50fe-522f-a333-7bba287e5b23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2u\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce329a3c-d6dc-516e-8f1d-f962832405f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305688} :answer-field/id #uuid "e243c6fc-094b-525d-978b-2c3f8f5a01d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305686}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "24bb40b1-a7b7-5eea-a633-757e31425152" :question/math-academy-id "q-32860" :question/problem "If $g(u)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡u \\\\ 5 \\\\ {u}^{2}\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t$, then  $(g∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(u) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\operatorname{ln}⁡u \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\,\\,5\\,\\, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\,\\,{u}^{2}\\,\\,\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{u} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2u\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)=\\frac{1}{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(g∘u)^{′}(t) & =g′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{u(t)} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2u(t)\\end{aligned}]{u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305692 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a146d5d3-2562-5b8b-886e-4cf6519d3282" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Chain Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51a6f446-26c9-5cf0-aa92-48ea3c2c01b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,0,\\,-2{e}^{2t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305694} {:answer/id #uuid "48c9cf06-5155-534b-94d5-3460987103d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,0,\\,-2{e}^{-2t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305695} {:answer/id #uuid "da588f43-0186-5c7d-b8cc-759c93d2cd8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{-2t},\\,0,\\,{e}^{-4t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305696} {:answer/id #uuid "c81cf2d5-da0f-577f-b402-8d0d0b0fef74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{-2t},\\,0,\\,-{e}^{-4t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305697} {:answer/id #uuid "13fe3f9d-fcda-5a0d-b6c2-8ea7b22cb170" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,0,\\,2{e}^{2t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305698}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48c9cf06-5155-534b-94d5-3460987103d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,0,\\,-2{e}^{-2t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305695} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf2cfbcb-f670-5fa4-a986-b61b9f1f0188" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305693}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3070a9d8-58c0-56d5-a223-11b2e4bdf7ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-32869" :question/problem "If $g(u)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡u,\\,0,\\,\\frac{1}{u}⟩$ and $u(t)={e}^{2t}$, then $(g∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(g∘u)^{′}(t)=g′(u(t))u′(t)\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(u) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\operatorname{ln}⁡u,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}0,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\frac{1}{u})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{u},\\,0,\\,-\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{2t})=2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(g∘u)^{′}(t) & =g′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{u(t)},\\,0,\\,-\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}(t)}⟩{u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t}⟨\\frac{1}{{e}^{2t}},\\,0,\\,-\\frac{1}{({e}^{2t})^{2}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2{e}^{2t}}{{e}^{2t}},\\,0,\\,-\\frac{2{e}^{2t}}{{e}^{4t}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,0,\\,-2{e}^{-2t}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305699 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a146d5d3-2562-5b8b-886e-4cf6519d3282" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Chain Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6ef7c57-c032-526f-aa67-9b807706273d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i-8{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305701} {:answer/id #uuid "cb6f1b81-3a1c-50da-a2e3-89884eb7b89c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t{e}^{t+1}\\,i+2t{e}^{2t}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305702} {:answer/id #uuid "4df4329c-21d2-51a8-b053-05bb883f4820" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4t{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+8t{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305703} {:answer/id #uuid "4b6c3d1f-8052-5990-80a0-a5b0872c3f23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4t{e}^{t+1}\\,i+6t{e}^{2t}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305704} {:answer/id #uuid "76ca5026-3449-5cf6-9238-64cc4803d070" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t{e}^{2t+1}\\,i+2t{e}^{4t}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305705}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4df4329c-21d2-51a8-b053-05bb883f4820" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4t{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+8t{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305703} :answer-field/id #uuid "df0dcda6-9c3c-5e46-bfc9-36ecd5a93d63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305700}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9342327c-ff4e-553a-a4f4-0263c91cce83" :question/math-academy-id "q-33260" :question/problem "If $f(u)={e}^{u+1}\\,i+{e}^{2u}\\,j+\\frac{1}{e}\\,k$ and $u(t)=2{t}^{2}$ then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "By the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)=f′(u(t))u′(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({e}^{u+1})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({e}^{2u})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\frac{1}{e}\\,k \\\\  & ={e}^{u+1}\\,i+2{e}^{2u}\\,j+0\\,k \\\\  & ={e}^{u+1}\\,i+2{e}^{2t}\\,j \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2})=4t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & =f′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\ (f∘u)^{′}(t) & =({e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+2{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j)4t \\\\  & =4t{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+8t{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305706 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05484b82-e643-5284-8e00-d4814d2288e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4\\sqrt{t},\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,8t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305708} {:answer/id #uuid "a6d5b0f9-2539-56b6-9648-0c55489f2f55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1+\\sqrt{t}}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,16{t}^{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305709} {:answer/id #uuid "470c60d0-d3cc-5b8c-a4e2-3b13f679e832" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2\\sqrt{t},\\,\\frac{{t}^{2}+1}{t},\\,2{t}^{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305710} {:answer/id #uuid "248144a4-5195-507c-8ead-000ee1a6fcf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{t-4}{{t}^{2}},\\,4{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305711} {:answer/id #uuid "b3341c7a-9b22-5378-a166-37514edd7b41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1+8\\sqrt{t}}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{t-4}{{t}^{2}},\\,16{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305712}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3341c7a-9b22-5378-a166-37514edd7b41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1+8\\sqrt{t}}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{t-4}{{t}^{2}},\\,16{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305712} :answer-field/id #uuid "83f07d3e-2650-56d7-8ae3-434d0181b857" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305707}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6942209a-90ad-5fb0-92e6-b66937204d70" :question/math-academy-id "q-70681" :question/problem "Differentiate $f(t)+4g(t)$ with respect to $t$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨\\sqrt{t},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2⟩ \\\\ g(t) & =⟨t,\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,{t}^{4}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f(t)+4g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)+4{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,4{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+4g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+4{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,0⟩+4⟨1,\\,-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,4{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,0⟩+⟨4,\\,-\\frac{4}{{t}^{2}},\\,16{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}+4,\\,\\frac{1}{t}-\\frac{4}{{t}^{2}},\\,0+16{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1+8\\sqrt{t}}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{t-4}{{t}^{2}},\\,16{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305713 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b19f5f01-948e-5f44-8016-63073ed31dbc" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Scalar Function Multiple Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37e660d1-908e-5666-b5d8-ca26033bf504" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{3}{{t}^{3}}+3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305715} {:answer/id #uuid "37438a7a-6ec2-5c6b-a483-3116933fb3ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}t+\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ {t}^{2}+2 \\\\ {t}^{3}+3t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305716} {:answer/id #uuid "ebea4dd2-a8e6-5c3d-88b1-c9f0f7b3149d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}t+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{2}+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305717} {:answer/id #uuid "2c0f1574-1851-5686-8819-5ccd95e3ed2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ 3t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ 4{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305718} {:answer/id #uuid "2e7c6caa-889e-5dc8-b553-a6ecbb6f8a56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ t+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{2}+3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305719}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e7c6caa-889e-5dc8-b553-a6ecbb6f8a56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ t+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{2}+3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305719} :answer-field/id #uuid "a25d6d17-d8b2-5b92-bde2-a8f121e43643" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305714}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a2951dd3-82c4-5618-8df7-28388cc279c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-70685" :question/problem "Find $(u(t)f(t))^{′}$ where $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ {t}^{2} \\\\ {t}^{3}\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(u(t)f(t))^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2t \\\\ 3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)=\\frac{1}{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)f(t))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ {t}^{2} \\\\ {t}^{3}\\end{aligned}]+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2t \\\\ 3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ t \\\\ {t}^{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ 2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ 3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ t+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{2}+3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305720 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b19f5f01-948e-5f44-8016-63073ed31dbc" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Scalar Function Multiple Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "611ca792-d600-5e6f-99a1-3a89dd0cde64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10t-8 \\\\ 12t-4 \\\\ 6t-5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305722} {:answer/id #uuid "8ba29446-9aa3-5adf-a382-bb1b9ff76751" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12t-15 \\\\ 14t-7 \\\\ 18t-2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305723} {:answer/id #uuid "14784451-5ea7-55a7-b322-97172ecb01e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8t-14 \\\\ 6t-5 \\\\ 10t-3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305724} {:answer/id #uuid "a372e0b5-6844-5cdf-a406-2261db425471" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4t-7 \\\\ 3t-2 \\\\ 5t-1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305725} {:answer/id #uuid "b531760c-4b94-52f4-8341-0dbfbb12cd4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}16t-14 \\\\ 12t-5 \\\\ 20t-3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305726}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b531760c-4b94-52f4-8341-0dbfbb12cd4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}16t-14 \\\\ 12t-5 \\\\ 20t-3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305726} :answer-field/id #uuid "53a4f43c-f2c7-554a-9b2f-7a24129f32d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305721}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "de33fa52-4e1e-55d5-aa30-80045075815d" :question/math-academy-id "q-71225" :question/problem "Find ${(u(t)f(t))}^{′}$ where $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}4t-1 \\\\ 3t+2 \\\\ 5t+6\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)=2t-3.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n{(u(t)f(t))}^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t+2) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5t+6)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-3)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u(t)f(t))}^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}4t-1 \\\\ 3t+2 \\\\ 5t+6\\end{aligned}]+(2t-3)[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8t-2 \\\\ 6t+4 \\\\ 10t+12\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}8t-12 \\\\ 6t-9 \\\\ 10t-15\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}16t-14 \\\\ 12t-5 \\\\ 20t-3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305727 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b19f5f01-948e-5f44-8016-63073ed31dbc" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Scalar Function Multiple Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "752c3c4b-c122-5bab-a102-13da626da5bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{3t} \\\\ 4{e}^{4t} \\\\ 5{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305729} {:answer/id #uuid "5e22929e-7749-5459-871c-149716ff3b0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}(t+3){e}^{3t} \\\\ (t+4){e}^{4t} \\\\ (t+5){e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305730} {:answer/id #uuid "27660b59-ff99-575e-8ae7-fc60725e2abe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 4t{e}^{4t} \\\\ 5t{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305731} {:answer/id #uuid "894798f4-fd12-5a14-87da-7676425ed204" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}({t}^{2}+1){e}^{3t} \\\\ ({t}^{2}+2){e}^{4t} \\\\ ({t}^{2}+3){e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305732} {:answer/id #uuid "c10cc291-7046-5aaf-a322-66066122c9be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}(3t+1){e}^{3t} \\\\ (4t+1){e}^{4t} \\\\ (5t+1){e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305733}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c10cc291-7046-5aaf-a322-66066122c9be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}(3t+1){e}^{3t} \\\\ (4t+1){e}^{4t} \\\\ (5t+1){e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305733} :answer-field/id #uuid "40a59066-0f8c-58ca-863d-11542afa86dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305728}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3a49de4c-5d1f-5ca3-aa1a-4ebaca430818" :question/math-academy-id "q-71227" :question/problem "Find ${(u(t)f(t))}^{′}$ where $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} \\\\ {e}^{4t} \\\\ {e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)=t.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n{(u(t)f(t))}^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{3t}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{4t}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{5t})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{3t} \\\\ 4{e}^{4t} \\\\ 5{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u(t)f(t))}^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} \\\\ {e}^{4t} \\\\ {e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{3t} \\\\ 4{e}^{4t} \\\\ 5{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} \\\\ {e}^{4t} \\\\ {e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 4t{e}^{4t} \\\\ 5t{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(3t+1){e}^{3t} \\\\ (4t+1){e}^{4t} \\\\ (5t+1){e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305734 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b19f5f01-948e-5f44-8016-63073ed31dbc" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Scalar Function Multiple Rule for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6aeeda8b-f3e7-50f2-a525-f9cb1e45a466" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{3}{e}^{t} \\\\ -16t \\\\ -{t}^{3}{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305736} {:answer/id #uuid "c09beb1e-6b5c-56d7-b309-e875013fcead" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}(2t+{t}^{2}){e}^{t} \\\\ 16t \\\\ (2t-{t}^{2}){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305737} {:answer/id #uuid "832905e6-89d2-51f6-bbcf-7292d3c655a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}({t}^{2}+{t}^{3}){e}^{t} \\\\ 4t \\\\ {t}^{3}{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305738} {:answer/id #uuid "f83193ff-79e3-5957-8133-1271d5f93bc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}(1-{t}^{2}){e}^{t} \\\\ 8t \\\\ (t+{t}^{2}){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305739} {:answer/id #uuid "b5cf90ca-8fb4-531d-84f4-9a72ecd5ecd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3t{e}^{t} \\\\ -8t \\\\ -3t{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305740}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c09beb1e-6b5c-56d7-b309-e875013fcead" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}(2t+{t}^{2}){e}^{t} \\\\ 16t \\\\ (2t-{t}^{2}){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305737} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1767873-42c2-57e8-b756-71d928f53399" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305735}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9d3825fa-4a39-5efb-9247-5f4f19ce4d38" :question/math-academy-id "q-71230" :question/problem "Find ${(u(t)f(t))}^{′}$ where $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 8 \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)={t}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n{(u(t)f(t))}^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})=2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u(t)f(t))}^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =2t[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 8 \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]+{t}^{2}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2t{e}^{t} \\\\ 16t \\\\ 2t{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{t}^{2}{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(2t+{t}^{2}){e}^{t} \\\\ 16t \\\\ (2t-{t}^{2}){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
